# TODO - Exact and diagnostic cycle detection

## Objective

Provide optional repeated-state detection using collision-safe confirmation for
exact results and clearly label probabilistic hash-only diagnostics.

## Acceptance

- Exact detection proves repeated full semantic state when feasible, while
  diagnostic approximations are clearly labeled and can never claim a proof from
  a lossy state key.
- The verifier is tested against valid cases and deliberately mutated invalid
  cases so acceptance and rejection boundaries are evidenced independently.
- The declared scope contains no unresolved placeholder implementation or
  undocumented workaround required for this objective to function.
- Evidence is durable enough to move this TODO to `docs/todo/completed/` and
  remove the exact TODO heading without losing unfinished intent.

## Evidence

- `src/runtime/virtual-machine/domain/cycle.rs` implements exact full-state
  confirmation and separately typed hash-only diagnostics.
- `tests/vm/cycle_detection.rs` forces key collisions over real complete VM
  checkpoints and proves deterministic exact replay.
- Profile checkpoints and a seeded register mutation remain distinct under a
  forced key collision until complete state equality is observed.
- Prerequisite completion evidence: `safe-rust-malbolge-vm`.
- **Completion:** Completed on 2026-08-06 after exact full-state
  confirmation, separately typed hash-only diagnostics, forced key collisions,
  classic and profile checkpoints, seeded state mutation, deterministic replay,
  Clippy, VM tests, and Jig validation passed.
